BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:diwali-20261108@todaycelebrates.com
DTSTAMP:20261014T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:Diwali
DESCRIPTION:Diwali is the festival of lights: five days in autumn marked by
  Hindus\, Jains\, Sikhs and some Buddhists\, and named for the Sanskrit di
 pavali\, a row of lamps. Its date is set by a lunisolar calendar rather th
 an the Gregorian one\, so it moves between mid-October and mid-November. I
 n the United States it has recently become a legislated holiday as well as
  a domestic one — New York City closes its public schools for it\, and P
 ennsylvania has designated a state Diwali Day\, though without requiring a
 nyone to close.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/diwali/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/diwali/
CATEGORIES:Celebration
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
